  "worked_solution": "To express the number in Cartesian form, we expand the parentheses and substitute the values of the cosine and sine.\n\nFirst, we find $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})$ and $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the values and expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =6\\sqrt{3}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{4\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}(-\\frac{1}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\text{i}\\,\\frac{18}{2} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{3}-9\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
